From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: the two IOMMUs

Describe IOMMU0 and IOMMU1 for the driver of `iommu-sun60i-add-the-allwinner-a733-iommu-driver`, with the clocks and
resets of `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-iommu-gates-and-resets`. No consumer yet; `arm64-dts-a733-display-engine-behind-iommu1` puts the display engine behind
IOMMU1.

  reg         per the A733 user manual: IOMMU0 0x03900000, IOMMU1
              0x03910000, 64 KiB each.
  interrupts  per the A733 user manual: INTID 202 / 203 =
              GIC SPI 170 / 171, level high.
  clocks      IOMMUn_BGR_REG bits 0-2 and MBUS_MAT_CLK_GATING bit 0 / 1.
  resets      IOMMUn_BGR_REG bit 16.
  #iommu-cells  1, the master index within the IOMMU: IOMMU0 USB0_USB1 0,
              CSI 1, ISP 2, VE_ENC 3; IOMMU1 VE_MBUS0 0, VE_MBUS1 1, DE0 2,
              DI 3, G2D 4, EINK 5. The block counts,
              four and six, were read on silicon (2026-09-15).

⚠ TWO NODES, WHERE THE VENDOR HAS ONE. The vendor DT describes both IOMMUs
as one node with reg 0x20000, a second cell for bypass, and master numbers
running 0-11 across both; its driver writes every global register to both
blocks. The hardware has two register blocks, two interrupts, two gate sets
and two resets, and a page table per TTB register -- so two nodes, two
iommu groups, and each IOMMU keeps its own table. The one-node form is also
what made the vendor call the display engine "master 8" (6 + 2).

What a node without a consumer does: the driver probes, de-asserts a reset
that already reads de-asserted, reads VERSION, and registers. It writes no
IOMMU register until a device is attached, so IOMMU0's masters -- the USB
host among them -- stay in bypass, their reset state.

A523 VALUE REJECTED: none taken. sun55i-a523.dtsi in 6.18.36 has no IOMMU
node (searched for "iommu" over arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/: only the H6,
H616 and our A733 files match), and the mainline binding files the A523
under the H616 fallback compatible, i.e. the H6 register layout; the driver patch
`iommu-sun60i-add-the-allwinner-a733-iommu-driver` shows that the A733 does not use that layout.

VERIFIED HERE: applies with fuzz 0 on top of the full series; the dtb built
with cpp + dtc carries iommu@3900000 and iommu@3910000 with the values
above.

HARDWARE-PROVEN on the 8 GiB board 2026-09-18, with a test build of this
series: both nodes bind
sun60i-a733-iommu -- 3900000.iommu and 3910000.iommu each carry the driver in
sysfs -- and each prints "version 0x16, ENABLE 0x0, TTB 0x0" at probe, so both
windows and both interrupts describe real blocks.

NOT RUN: a build without `arm64-dts-a733-display-engine-behind-iommu1` (these nodes without a consumer).
The full series was booted instead. What that build would have added is covered
in the same boot by IOMMU0, which has no consumer: it probes, keeps ENABLE 0
and TTB 0, leaves its four masters in bypass, and USB is unaffected.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -1027,6 +1027,61 @@
 		};
 
 		/*
+		 * The two IOMMUs (UM chapter 10). Each translates for its own
+		 * masters through its own page table; the cell of `iommus` is
+		 * the master index:
+		 *
+		 *   iommu0  USB0_USB1 0, CSI 1, ISP 2, VE_ENC 3
+		 *   iommu1  VE_MBUS0 0, VE_MBUS1 1, DE0 2, DI 3, G2D 4, EINK 5
+		 *
+		 * (four and six master blocks read on
+		 * silicon on 2026-09-15.)
+		 *
+		 *
+		 *   reg         the memory map of the A733 user manual: IOMMU0 0x03900000, IOMMU1
+		 *               0x03910000, 64 KiB each.
+		 *               ⚠ The vendor DT describes both as ONE node,
+		 *               reg 0x20000; its driver writes every global register to
+		 *               both blocks. Two nodes is what the hardware has:
+		 *               two register blocks, two interrupts, two gate
+		 *               sets and two resets.
+		 *   interrupts  INTID 202/203 = SPI 170/171
+		 *               (A733 user manual).
+		 *   clocks      IOMMUn_BGR_REG bits 0-2 and MBUS_MAT_CLK_GATING
+		 *               bit 0/1, all CLK_IS_CRITICAL (`clk-sunxi-ng-a733-iommu-gates-and-resets` says why).
+		 *   resets      IOMMUn_BGR_REG bit 16.
+		 *
+		 * No consumer on iommu0: its masters stay in bypass, which is
+		 * their reset state, and the driver writes nothing to a block
+		 * without a translating master.
+		 */
+		iommu0: iommu@3900000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-iommu";
+			reg = <0x0 0x03900000 0x0 0x10000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 170 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_IOMMU0_SYS_MCLK>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_IOMMU0_SYS_PCLK>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_IOMMU0_SYS_HCLK>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU0>;
+			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_IOMMU0>;
+			#iommu-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
+		iommu1: iommu@3910000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-iommu";
+			reg = <0x0 0x03910000 0x0 0x10000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 171 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_IOMMU1_SYS_MCLK>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_IOMMU1_SYS_PCLK>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_IOMMU1_SYS_HCLK>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU1>;
+			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_IOMMU1>;
+			#iommu-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
+		/*
 		 * PCK-600 power controller (Arm CoreLink PCK-600 / PPU). Provides
 		 * the SoC power domains; PD_USB2 (index 8) is boot-on (on silicon,
 		 * the 8 GiB board: status @0x07068008 = 0x8). Attach-only driver variant
